@startuml Authentication Flow

' ============================================================================
' Authentication Flow Diagram
' ============================================================================
' This diagram shows how Bearer Token authentication works in the API.
' All endpoints (except /health) require a valid token in the Authorization header.
'
' Token verification process:
' 1. Extract Bearer token from Authorization header
' 2. Hash the token using SHA256
' 3. Look up the hash in the api_tokens table
' 4. Validate: is_active=true, not expired
' 5. Update last_used_at timestamp
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2

title Bearer Token Authentication Flow (Database-backed)

actor "API Client" as Client
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "HTTPBearer" as Bearer
participant "verify_token" as Auth
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Router" as Router

== Successful Authentication ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Auth : hash_token(token)\n(SHA256)
Auth -> DB : SELECT * FROM api_tokens\nWHERE token_hash = ?
DB --> Auth : ApiToken record
Auth -> Auth : Validate:\n- is_active = true\n- expires_at > now()
Auth -> DB : UPDATE last_used_at
Auth --> Bearer : Valid (ApiTokenEntity)
Bearer --> API : Authenticated
API -> Router : Process request
Router --> Client : 200 OK

== Invalid Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer wrong-token
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Auth : hash_token(token)
Auth -> DB : SELECT * FROM api_tokens\nWHERE token_hash = ?
DB --> Auth : NULL (not found)
Auth --> Client : 401 Unauthorized\n"Invalid authentication token"

== Expired Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer expired-token
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Auth : hash_token(token)
Auth -> DB : SELECT * FROM api_tokens\nWHERE token_hash = ?
DB --> Auth : ApiToken (expires_at < now)
Auth -> Auth : expires_at < now()?
Auth --> Client : 401 Unauthorized\n"Token has expired"

== Deactivated Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer deactivated-token
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Auth : hash_token(token)
Auth -> DB : SELECT * FROM api_tokens\nWHERE token_hash = ?
DB --> Auth : ApiToken (is_active = false)
Auth -> Auth : is_active = false?
Auth --> Client : 401 Unauthorized\n"Token has been deactivated"

== Missing Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nNo Authorization header
API -> Bearer : No token found
Bearer --> Client : 403 Forbidden

note right of DB
  **api_tokens table:**
  - id, name
  - token_hash (SHA256)
  - is_active
  - created_at
  - expires_at
  - last_used_at
end note

note right of Auth
  **Security Features:**
  - SHA256 hash comparison
  - Token expiration support
  - Soft delete (is_active)
  - Usage tracking
end note

note left of Client
  **Token Management:**
  POST /tokens - Create new
  GET /tokens - List all
  DELETE /tokens/{id} - Remove
  POST /tokens/{id}/deactivate
end note

@enduml
